  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mandanapu Supriya vs The State Of Telangana on 23 February, 2022 Author: P.Naveen Rao Bench: P Naveen Rao, G.Radha Rani The Hon'Ble Sri Justice P. Naveen Rao And The Hon'Ble Smt Dr. Justice G. Radha Rani Writ Petition No. 29178 Of 2021 Date: 23.02.2022 Between: Mandanapu Supriya, W/o. Mandapu Subash, Aged 30 years, Occ: Housewife, R/o. H.No. 5-52, Tadvai, kamram, Warangal District, Telangana State. .....Petitioner And The State of Telangana, Rep by its., Principal Secretary, General Administration (Spl. (Law and Order) Department, Secretariat, Hyderabad and others. .....Respondents The Court made the following: -2- The Hon'Ble Sri Justice P. Naveen Rao And The Hon'Ble Smt Dr. Justice G. Radha Rani Writ Petition No. 29178 Of 2021 Order:",
    "facts": "This writ petition is filed by the wife of detenue- Mandanapu Subash, challenging the detention order dated 03.09.2021 made under Section 3(2) of the Telangana Prevention of Dangerous Activities of Bootleggers, Dacoits, Drug-Offenders, Goondas, Immoral Traffic Offenders, Land Grabbers, Spurious Seed Offenders, Insecticide Offenders, Fertiliser Offenders, Food Adulteration Offenders, Fake Document Offenders, Scheduled Commodities Offenders, Forest Offenders, Gaming Offenders, Sexual Offenders, Explosive Substances Offenders, Arms Offenders, Cyber Crime Offenders and White Collar or Financial Offenders Act, 1986 (Act 1 of 1986) as confirmed by the Government vide G.O.Rt.No.2565 dated 18.11.2021. 4. The detenue was arrested on 19.05.2021, by the time the order of detention was passed, he was in judicial custody. 5. The order of detention refers to four crimes registered against the detenue. Crime No.127 of 2020 was registered under Section 457 and 380 of Indian Penal Code (IPC) in Madikonda Police Station. Crime No.109 of 2021 was registered under Section 454 and 380 of IPC in Inthezargunj Police Station. Crime No.79 of 2021 was registered under Section 394, 454 of IPC and 102 of Code of Criminal Procedure (Cr.PC) in Geesugonda Police Station. Crime No.115 of 2021 was registered under Section 379 of IPC in Geesugonda Police Station. 6. In all the four crimes the allegations were regarding breaking open the lock of the door, committing theft of gold ornaments, cash. In addition, in Crime No.79 of 2021, beating the complainant and theft of mobile phone of complainant was also alleged. 7. All these crimes can be investigated and prosecuted in the normal course of enforcement of law and order.",
